the 17 year old who video recorded  george floyd's murder  is going to receive an honorary pulitzer  prize and i think this is a great  development so many people  felt powerless in the face of what was  happening to george floyd and others and  darnell fraser  who was only 17 at the time stood her  ground and recorded things she was  walking home with her nine-year-old  cousin  when she had the bravery to sit there  and record everything happening  of course many people wanted to  intervene but the fact of the matter is  if you intervene in a situation like  that you might be  charged with obstruction of justice or  assaulting a police officer  and it's not fair but those are the  rules  and what people can do is when they see  something that might be suspicious it's  not clear  simply record the police record the  activity that's what you can do as a  citizen to prevent these kinds of things  from happening in the future  it's sad but true but the conviction of  derek shovin probably wouldn't have  happened without the video evidence and  we should be encouraging citizen  journalists like this as much as we can
 

